t
o


the policeman






Ich habe 
meinem Freund
 das Buch geliehen


{


I lent
 
m
y friend




 the book


I lent the book
 
to my friend








(b)
 
Some verbs take a sole object in the dative case
These are intransitive verbs which do not have a direct object in the accusative case, but only a dative object. The English equivalents are most often simple transitive verbs, e.g.:







Er hat 
seiner Tante
 für ihre Hilfe gedankt


He thanked
 
his aunt


 for her help






Der Einbrecher hat 
dem alten Mann
 mit einer Pistole gedroht


The burglar threatened
 
the old man


 with a pistol








Other verbs like this are 
dienen
,
 folgen
,
