(c)
 
The dative case can mark a person from whose standpoint an action is being judged
This usage typically involves an adjective qualified by 
zu
 or 
genug
:







Mir
 vergeht die Zeit zu schnell


I have a feeling that time is passing too quickly






Fährt sie 
dir
 schnell genug?


Is she driving fast enough for you?








A similar dative of the person concerned is frequent with the verb 
sein
 and a noun. In such cases, English uses a phrase with ‘to’ or ‘for’:








Das Wiedersehen mit dir war 
mir
mir
 ein Vergnügen


