(c)
 
The dative case with
 
sein
 
and
 
werden
 
and adjectives expressing sensations
With a number of adjectives which express a sensation used with the verbs 
sein
 and 
werden
, the person who is experiencing the sensation is put into the dative case in an impersonal construction. In English the person is typically the subject of the verb:







