noun of measurement + adjective + noun
. With masculine and neuter nouns in the singular, as in the first example above, it is typical of formal written registers and largely limited to them, but it is quite frequent in the plural in both written and spoken German.


(c)
 
Usage when the noun of measurement is in the dative case
Here usage is particularly uncertain and variable, and the following alternatives are equally acceptable:


(i)
 After nouns of measurement in -
er
, e.g. 
Zentner
 ‘hundredweight’, 
