codex
The reference sections confirm the seven distinct patterns: accusative objects/adverbials, fixed genitive time phrases, several dative roles, genitive-versus-*von*, case-matching apposition, and measurement-phrase apposition. I’m now writing the 82 translations and exercise-specific rationales, keeping all copied German confined to validated `<i>` spans.
