pgg-c02-e04-i1	the French wine; a French wine	Accusative: the requested item is the direct object; a masculine adjective takes -en after either article (§§2.2, 6.1).
pgg-c02-e04-i2	the light-colored beer; a light-colored beer	Accusative direct object: a neuter adjective takes -e after the definite article and -es after the indefinite (§§2.2, 6.1).
pgg-c02-e04-i3	the small cola; a small cola	Accusative: the requested item is the direct object; a feminine adjective takes -e after either article (§§2.2, 6.1).
pgg-c02-e04-i4	the fresh orange juice; some fresh orange juice	Accusative: the requested item is the direct object; a masculine adjective takes -en after either article (§§2.2, 6.1).
pgg-c02-e04-i5	the stylish shoes; stylish shoes	Accusative: the requested items are direct objects; a plural adjective takes -en after the definite article and -e without one (§§2.2, 6.1).
pgg-c02-e04-i6	the green glasses; a pair of green glasses	Accusative: the requested item is the direct object; a feminine adjective takes -e after either article (§§2.2, 6.1).
