Five samples:

1. `pgg-c02-e04-i1` — “the French wine; a French wine” — Accusative direct object with masculine adjective endings.
2. `pgg-c02-e05-i11` — “After he had waited almost a month…” — Accusative duration plus genitive indefinite time.
3. `pgg-c02-e12-i6` — “Maditha cut her finger.” — Possessive dative with a prepositional body part.
4. `pgg-c02-e09-i10` — “some of her funds” — Required *von*-partitive.
5. `pgg-c02-e17-i2` — “two hundred tonnes of Russian iron ore” — Dative measurement-phrase apposition.

Commit creation was unavailable because `.git` is read-only in this environment.
